      "widgets_values": [
        "VEHICLE IDENTITY: ARES-01 is a large unmanned Mars science rover, not a car, truck, or SUV. It has exactly six identical airless metallic mesh wheels: three on the left side and three on the right, arranged as front, middle, and rear wheel stations. Each wheel has an open woven titanium-mesh structure, deep chevron tread bands, and a dark metallic hub. Low elongated rectangular chassis with angular white and light-gray protective panels. True six-wheel rocker-bogie suspension with clearly visible articulated linkages connecting all three wheel stations. Tall central camera mast with a rectangular stereo-camera head. One folded articulated robotic arm mounted on the front-right of the chassis. Compact high-gain antenna at the rear. Flat dark equipment deck covering the upper body. Subtle red ARES-01 mission markings. Functional aerospace engineering, scientifically plausible, realistic materials, no decorative fantasy or science-fiction technology. No pneumatic tires, no solid rubber automobile wheels, no hidden middle wheels, and never a four-wheel configuration. Preserve this exact design."
      ],
      "title": "Vehicle identity - keep stable"
    },
